Atlantic Canada QSO Party -- entries used by a station in New Brunswick, Nova Scotia, Prince Edward Island or Newfoundland and Labrador
The 47 counties and divisions, each counting as its province, then DC as Maryland, the 50 states and the other 9 provinces and territories.
The county file comes FIRST, so a county code wins over any state alias spelled the same.
DC is mapped to Md before s50.dom: the sponsor rules say count DC as MD.
The provinces are written here and P12/P13 are not included: their call-area aliases would let the rover strip take a call such as
W1AW/VE1, and NB, NS, PE and NL are not received exchanges here (an Atlantic Canada station sends its five-letter code), so those
four carry a display name only. The class keeps a county's province on the PREFIX sheet, per band and mode, not here.
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.

INCLUDE FILE acqp_cty.dom
Dc > Md = DC
INCLUDE FILE s50.dom
Qc = QC,^Quebec
On = ON,^Ontario
Mb = MB,^Manitoba
Sk = SK,^Saskatchewan
Ab = AB,^Alberta
Bc = BC,^British Columbia
Nt = NT,^Northwest Territories
Nu = NU,^Nunavut
Yt = YT,^Yukon
Nb = ^New Brunswick
Ns = ^Nova Scotia
Pe = ^Prince Edward Island
Nl = ^Newfoundland and Labrador
